KNOWNBUG
shared-loop-variable5.sv
--bound 0
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.a == main\.b: PROVED up to bound 0$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^file .* line \d+: `Verilog::\$root\.main\.i' has multiple drivers$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
As shared-loop-variable4.sv, but the loop index is declared 'reg
[31:0]'. Because the exemption in verilog_rtl_buildert::commit keys on
ID_C_verilog_type == ID_integer, a 'reg'-typed loop index is not
exempted and the benign shared counter is still rejected (the '--'
section below is the current, buggy output). Desired behaviour is
PROVED.
